version: "2.0"
description: >-
  Gnomon voice (docs/specs/gnomon.md §14; the spec node #gnomon-voice is the
  kernel-supervised voice child and is not built yet). This directory holds
  its first native piece, the darwin audio I/O binary (TD-2026-10-19-298,
  slice V2b, T-2026-10-19-026): io-darwin/ is a SwiftPM package (swift-tools
  5.9, macOS 14), scripts/build-voice-io.mjs bundles and signs it as
  GnomonVoiceIO.app (bin/, gitignored; checksums.json after a signed build).
  PROBES.md holds the founder's P1 (TCC attribution) and P7 (AEC leak) steps.
  macOS only: CI builds and tests it on the macOS runner of the native job,
  never on Windows or Linux.

components:
  gnomon-voice:
    description: >-
      The voice client core in Node, @a-company/gnomon-voice (spec §14, slice
      V2c, TD-2026-10-19-298, T-2026-10-19-026). V2e: the kernel spawns it
      as `gnomon-voice run --fd 3 --home H --io P`; fd 3 is a socketpair
      already authenticated as the talk-only voice principal p:<ns>/voice
      (FdRpc speaks gnomon-rpc:v1 NDJSON over it; no hello, no key here), and
      the run ends when stdin ends or the link closes. It reads the
      attachment and the human's ceiling from status.voice, and runs modes
      OFF, PTT and AMBIENT (it may narrow the mode locally, never widen it).
      It speaks only the kernel's voice.turn.agent{source:'kernel-speakable'}
      rows (never turn.event, never its own playback rows) and logs its
      playback windows as voice.turn.agent{t0, t1, textPlanned, textSpoken}.
      Ctrl-Alt-M toggles the mic locally; Ctrl-Alt-A switches ambient and
      push-to-talk within the ceiling, and above it only relays a notice
      for the GUI (request.voice.report{notice: {text, code}}, never a log
      row). The principal comes from status.voice.principal (no flag).
      Dictation (TD-2026-10-20-262): delivery 'composer' (default; the
      kernel-spawned run) never calls session.send and appends
      voice.turn.user forwarded:false (the kernel stamps forwardable; the
      GUI composer sends a push-to-talk draft after a countdown, an ambient
      draft only on a key press); --delivery direct keeps the old forward for
      headless use, for PUSH-TO-TALK turns only. TD-2026-10-20-125: ambient
      speech never sends itself (dictated under either delivery; the kernel
      refuses a direct non-ptt send voice-off{cause: composer}). Activity edges only, as
      request.voice.report{dictation: {activity speaking|transcribing|idle,
      holdToggles}}; the Ctrl-Alt-H hold-toggle hotkey increments
      holdToggles.
      Capture (T-2026-10-20-005 A1/A2, TD-2026-10-20-086): one state machine
      per segment, idle -> hearing (PTT key-down; AMBIENT VAD start) ->
      transcribing -> captured | dropped{reason}, the closed reasons
      too-short, echo, not-attached, no-words, not-enrolled, barge-in,
      refused set at each drop site; reported as
      request.voice.report{capture: {state, segId, reason?, level?}} on the
      serialized reports chain, non-terminal at most 5 Hz (latest wins),
      terminal always, hearing re-reported every second (the kernel TTL is
      5 s). level is 0..1 from the binary's level events (levelOf: -60..0
      dBFS), sent on hearing reports only. No words in A1. Aegis L4: a
      waiting capture report of the same segment and state is replaced by
      the newest (no backlog behind a slow kernel); edges and terminal
      states are always queued in order.
      Live words (B1, T-2026-10-20-005, V1-V5 in TD-2026-10-20-086,
      src/partials.ts): while hearing, the open segment is buffered in memory
      with up to 300 ms of pre-roll; every 600 ms of heard audio one tick decodes a
      window (from the segment start up to 6 s, then about 4 s with its head
      anchored at a committed word boundary, never sliding freely, capped at
      8 s) with SttEngine.transcribeWords (sherpa decodeAsync, word starts
      from tokens + timestamps). ONE decode in flight: a busy tick (or a
      running final transcription) is skipped, never queued.
      LocalAgreement-2 (LiveAgreement): words two consecutive decodes agree
      on are committed and never shrink; a flip inside the committed region
      commits nothing; trailing punctuation is stripped. V1 gate: no words
      until SpeakerVerifier.provisional matches an enrolled print on the
      first 1.5 s (PTT too); a non-match means no words for the segment.
      Words ride capture reports as text{committed, tail} (sanitised, newest
      600 chars) on hearing / transcribing only; never log.append rows,
      voice.turn.user or session.send. The final transcript stays the
      full-segment decode. SherpaStt decodes are serialized and async
      (decodeAsync; in the B0 bench on an Apple M4, n = 10, the sync decode
      blocked the loop for the whole decode, p50 202 to 232 ms).
      Aegis L2: a decode past STT_DECODE_WATCHDOG_MS (plus the audio length)
      is rejected, the recognizer rebuilt and the event logged. Aegis L3: the
      sanitiser also strips tag characters, variation selectors and Hangul
      fillers (client and kernel).
      Table talk system voice (TD-2026-10-20-294, src/earcon.ts): kernel
      speakable items with from:'kernel' (ask-waiting, edits) are said by a
      different Kokoro speaker (SherpaTts systemSidFor, never the model's
      speaker) after a generated two-note earcon; model text (from block,
      heuristic or absent) never gets either. A kernel-speakable row is
      spoken only when its principal is p:<ns>/kernel (Aegis L1).
      Kernel-decided enrolment (src/enrol-watch.ts): while running it polls
      status (1.5 s); on status.voice.enrolment phase 'requested' it pauses
      the voice loop, turns the mic on for the recording if it was off,
      records the three ENROL_PHRASES (shared with the GUI dialog; the report
      carries no phrase text), stores the print (0700 dir, 0600 file) and
      reports ready, recording, recorded (phrase 0-based, of 3), then done,
      or failed with the reason (mic off and not turnable on, no speech).
      Build: tsup (splitting off), then scripts/voice-manifest.mjs writes
      dist/voice-client.manifest.json (sha256 of every dist file and
      voice-models.manifest.json); the gnomon build stamp pins its hash.
      Aegis M1: SpawnedAudioIO spawns gnomon-voice-io with IO_CHILD_STDIO
      (pipe, pipe, inherit, ignore): fd 3, the kernel link, never reaches the
      io binary (a test falsifies it against a real socket on fd 3).
      Engines come
      from sherpa-onnx-node 1.13.8, an optional native dependency: Silero VAD,
      Parakeet TDT 0.6B v2 int8, Kokoro-82M int8 en and 3D-Speaker CAM++
      speaker embeddings. Every engine is injected through the AudioIO,
      VadEngine, SttEngine, TtsEngine, SpeakerEngine and KernelLink
      interfaces. SpawnedAudioIO speaks gnomon-voice-io:v1 to the V2b binary.
      It refuses to capture unless the binary says disclaimed === true
      (fail closed), drops frames after mic off, spawns the binary with an
      allow-list env, and takes the aec claim and the transport from the
      route event. FakeAudioIO plays WAV fixtures. voice-models.manifest.json
      pins each model's URL, sha256 and size, and the sha256 and size of
      every archive member. `models fetch [--json] [--from <dir>]` verifies
      every download into ~/.gnomon/voice/models (0700), extracts with
      tar --no-same-owner, refuses symlinks, non-regular and unpinned
      members, and every model file is re-hashed against the manifest
      before it is loaded. Prints are embeddings only, stored in voice/prints/<name>/.
      Speaker front end (founder regression 2026-10-20): every CAM++
      embedding passes the speech gate speechOnly (speech-gate:v1: frames
      of GATE_FRAME_MS, quiet below max(GATE_FLOOR_DBFS, peak -
      GATE_REL_DB); edge quiet and inner pauses of GATE_PAUSE_MS or longer
      cut), so the quiet around speech never moves it. A print records its
      frontEnd; prints from another front end are never compared and are
      reported as request.voice.report{prints:{stale}} (status.voice.prints;
      the GUI nudges "Re-teach Gnomon your voice") with ONE notice per run.
      Fail closed: VERIFY_THRESHOLD 0.65 and no verify under
      MIN_VERIFY_SPEECH_MS of gated speech (MIN_PROVISIONAL_SPEECH_MS for
      live words, MIN_ENROL_SPEECH_MS per enrolment phrase). SherpaStt
      decode priority: a partial not started while a final waits returns []
      undecoded. SherpaVad.reset() restarts its sample counter (t0 skew
      fix). Verification is a convenience filter, not authentication (spec
      14.4.2).
      Audio is never written to disk (G-VOX-05).
    path: src/
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, voice, client, paradigm-8, v2c]
    flows: [$voice-turn]
  gnomon-voice-io:
    description: >-
      Hotkeys talk, mic-toggle, mode-toggle, hold-toggle (carbonId 4,
      default ctrl+alt+h, TD-2026-10-20-262 dictation hold) and stop-speaking
      (carbonId 5, default ctrl+alt+. — the period key, kVK_ANSI_Period 0x2F,
      spelled "." or "period"; T-2026-10-19-026: cuts the reply being read aloud).
      The voice child's audio I/O, mic only (no keychain group, no network,
      writes only stdout/stderr). Protocol gnomon-voice-io:v1, the same
      framing both ways: type:u8 length:u32le payload (max 1 MiB); 0x01 JSON
      (stdin commands, stdout replies and events), 0x02 capture (stdout:
      hostTimeNs:u64le sampleRate:u32le s16le, 16 kHz mono after voice
      processing), 0x03 playback (stdin: sampleRate:u32le s16le mono TTS,
      8-48 kHz). Commands info, mic.on, mic.off, play.stop (barge-in flush),
      play.end, route.get, hotkeys.set {bindings}, quit; each gets one reply
      {type:'reply', id, op, ok}. Events (tUs monotonic µs, the capture
      clock): ready, mic, route {route, aec: vpio|headphones|none}, level
      {rmsDBFS, peakDBFS} ~15 Hz, playback.start {audibleAtUs},
      playback.end {reason: drained|stopped|mic-switch|route-change|exit},
      hotkey {action: talk|mic-toggle|mode-toggle|hold-toggle|stop-speaking, phase: down|up}, engine,
      error, exit. Mic on = one AVAudioEngine with
      inputNode.setVoiceProcessingEnabled(true) (VoiceProcessingIO AEC) and
      a player node in the same engine, so TTS is the echo reference; mic
      off stops and releases that engine (no orange dot) and TTS plays via an
      output-only engine that never touches inputNode. Route from CoreAudio
      (default output device transport + built-in data source, listeners
      on both). Hotkeys via Carbon RegisterEventHotKey, press and release,
      no Input Monitoring; defaults ctrl+alt+space (talk), ctrl+alt+m,
      ctrl+alt+a; reported only, the controller acts. Mic modes re-spawn
      with TCC responsibility disclaimed so the Microphone grant names
      GnomonVoiceIO (probe P1; --no-disclaim is the control). Aegis V2b
      fixes: MicGate (a mic.off during an open TCC prompt wins, generation
      counter; mic.on refused not-disclaimed unless disclaimed or
      --no-disclaim), DisclaimToken (disclaimed only when argv
      --disclaim-token equals the env token; a stray env var is ignored),
      ParentWatch (kqueue EVFILT_PROC NOTE_EXIT on the re-spawning and the
      original parent: the child exits with either), re-spawn path from
      _NSGetExecutablePath + realpath only, a tap generation so no capture or
      level frame follows mic:false, a bounded stdout queue (one writer
      thread, no lock held in write(2), capture frames dropped first with a
      capture.dropped event), transport in mic and route events. --version,
      --selftest (1 s smoke), --probe-aec <file> (P7); stdin EOF exits 0.
      VoiceIOCore (frame codec, command parser, hotkey config, level and
      route math, mic gate, disclaim token, parent watch) is pure or
      Darwin-only and covered by swift test (37 XCTests).
    path: io-darwin/
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, voice, native, swift, paradigm-8, audio, v2b]
  gnomon-voice-io-build:
    description: >-
      scripts/build-voice-io.mjs: swift build -c release → GnomonVoiceIO.app
      (bundle id gnomon.voice-io, LSUIElement, NSMicrophoneUsageDescription
      "Gnomon voice listens only while the mic is on."), codesign
      --options runtime --timestamp with the one Developer ID Application
      identity of team SW4BMQ8PNL (looked up via the helper's signing.mjs),
      exactly one entitlement com.apple.security.device.audio-input, no
      provisioning profile and no keychain group; verifies --strict, the
      VOICE_IO_REQUIREMENT, the entitlement set and the runtime flag; sha256
      into checksums.json (advisory). --unsigned for CI. No notarization
      (founder-run).
    path: scripts/
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, voice, signing, build, v2b]
  gnomon-voice-bench-partials:
    description: >-
      scripts/bench-partials.mjs: the B0 benchmark for voice phase B (live
      words while speaking; T-2026-10-20-005, ruling V5 in
      TD-2026-10-20-086). Builds the Parakeet recognizer exactly as
      engines/sherpa.ts does (only numThreads varies), synthesises ~15 s of
      test speech in memory with Kokoro, and also uses the Parakeet archive's
      test_wavs/0.wav. It times 4, 6 and 8 s tail-window decodes at 2 and 4
      threads, measures sync decode against decodeAsync (event-loop block),
      checks a worker_thread, and measures prefix stability and
      LocalAgreement-2 commits for decodes every 600 ms. Read-only on the
      model home (verifiedModelPaths); it writes nothing. Results are in
      PROBES.md, section B0. Dev tool only, not shipped.
    path: scripts/
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, voice, benchmark, stt, phase-b]

flows:
  voice-turn:
    description: >-
      One spoken turn (spec §14.2). User side: AudioIO frames, then the PTT
      held span or a VAD segment, then the gates (attached, mode within the
      ceiling, outside every playback window plus 750 ms), then STT, then
      speaker verification, then log.append voice.turn.user{turnId,
      speakerId, speakerEnrolled, forwarded, mode, aec, aecTransport, t0,
      t1, text}, then session.send content [{text}] for enrolled speakers
      only. Unknown speakers are logged with no text. A refusal is shown
      and never retried. Agent side: log.read follow, then the speakable
      rows the kernel writes (voice.turn.agent{source: kernel-speakable,
      turnSeq, items}), then Kokoro one sentence at a time, then play, then
      voice.turn.agent{t0, t1, textPlanned, textSpoken}. Barge-in: speech
      past the barge-in threshold (configured), or the talk key, stops
      playback and drops the rest of the reply. Live words (B1): while a
      segment is heard, anchored tail-window decodes (decodeAsync, one in
      flight, busy ticks skipped) fold into LocalAgreement-2; after a
      provisional speaker match on the first 1.5 s they ride hearing /
      transcribing capture reports as text{committed, tail}, shown only in
      the GUI ghost line (gui credential); they never reach log.append,
      voice.turn.user or session.send, and the turn's text stays the
      full-segment decode.
    steps: ["#gnomon-voice", "#gnomon-voice-io"]

